            <ArticleTitle>Fractured and embolized coronary stent mimicking significant internal carotid stenosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>739-40</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe the case of 77-year-old woman who underwent five coronary angiographies in 9 months due to in-stent re-stenosis of Cypher-Stents, and who finally required coronary artery bypass grafting surgery. Preoperative investigations revealed a significant internal carotid stenosis, which was due to a fractured and embolized Cypher-Stent.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
